I wouldn't say easy, I'd say handleable, especially with
overpreparation.  The two main threats of liches (assuming MR) are
their ability to summon nasties and curse items.   Summon nasties can
be dealt with by a combination of conflict, scrolls of scare monster
(with backup scrolls in case of fire breathing), and wands of
teleport.  The cursing of items is not a big deal when you have a
virtually unlimited supply of holy water.  And of course the main
annoyance (or benefit) of liches is their tendency to flee to the
upstairs and I would just blindfold and when they teleported back to
me I would take their spot on the stairs.
